# Backend Standards

## Runtime & Framework
- Node.js 20 LTS
- Express 4 with TypeScript strict mode

## Route Handlers
- All routes use `async/await` with `try/catch` — no unhandled promise rejections:

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
router.get('/users', async (req, res) => {
  const users = await UserService.getAll();
  res.json(users);
});

// ✅ GOOD
router.get('/users', async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const users = await UserService.getAll();
    res.json(users);
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});
```

## Validation
- Validate all request bodies with **Zod** before processing — never trust raw `req.body`

## Async Jobs
- Use **BullMQ** for all async jobs
- Never process AI calls synchronously inside route handlers

## Security
- Rate limiting on **all** routes
- Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)
